  "description": "With no standby GPU a claim borrows a wall tile: the last tile in slot order that runs its current generation (not one relaunching). The tile keeps its place, is shown borrowed with no public frame URL and leaves its host's band (the agent gets no rect, only the private camera). The cap on lent tiles (default 2 or a tenth of the tiles, rounded up, whichever is smaller) refuses a second claim. A race leaves the borrowed tile alone and lists it as sitting out. When the claim ends the tile's VM restores back into the wall, timed like any relaunch.",
